ly narrow the margin.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "The District of Columbia is the most Democratic-leaning jurisdiction in the country, with a partisan lean of 44 points toward Democrats, and it has sided overwhelmingly with the Democratic presidential nominee in every election since home rule. With the incumbent president term-limited, this is an open-seat matchup between a generic Democrat and a generic Republican, and no competitive general election is expected.\n\nNo public polls or expert ratings are available for this race, so the forecast rests on fundamentals. Headlines point to an environment unfavorable to President Trump even in the most Democratic places, including the District itself, and local coverage shows Trump looming over District politics. The Democratic nominee is all but certain to carry the District's three electoral votes by a wide margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9995, "margin": 44.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 1.0, "margin": 44.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 1.0, "margin": 50.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9999, "margin": 50.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 1.0, "margin": 50.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9999, "margin": 52.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9989, "margin": 44.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9998, "margin": 50.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9997, "margin": 50.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9995, "margin": 47.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 44.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9989, "margin": 45.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9992, "margin": 45.0}]}